    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VvsAv9bMnVw5hmscGggixs)_\n\n## What\nText typed in `M-x` glitches and disappears in `vertico-posframe` (and did in `mini-frame`). Only `M-x` is nano-styled, so the suspects are the three nano parts in `sp-posframe`. The dotted line stays, as asked.\n\n- Prompt: `:inverse-video` and `:box` are replaced by explicit swapped colours (`sp-posframe--prompt-block`). The box makes the first line taller than the others, and reverse video in a child frame is a likely source of the invisible text (#121).\n- Dotted line: its overlay is now created like Vertico's own (empty, both markers advancing). Before, the front marker did not advance, so the overlay grew to cover the typed input.\n- The literate doc has a new section with checks to run in the open `M-x` and a list of hooks to remove one by one, to find the cause if this does not fix it.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The cause is a diagnosis from reading the code, not confirmed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBs9srTW9kUiGXduSF)_",
